  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Whisenhunt lasted 3.1 innings and San Diego didn't waste any time getting comfortable. Six runs crossed by the fourth. Game over, nothing left to learn.",
    "what_this_means": "The Giants brought six strikeouts and two hits to Petco Park. That's not baseball. That's surrender. Houser cleaned up the mess after the starter exited, throwing 4.2 scoreless innings in what amounted to extended garbage time. The bullpen's composure didn't matter because there was nothing to protect and no one hitting behind it. This is what happens when pitching fails early and the lineup never wakes up. Inconsistency isn't a pattern anymore. It's the team itself. They'll beat you one night and get beat 7-0 the next, and there's no reliable way to predict which version shows up.",
    "what_to_watch": "San Diego starts Walker Buehler tonight at 5:40 PM. Tyler Mahle has a 2.85 ERA over his last four starts and carries that into a game the Giants cannot afford to lose twice.",
